    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0473" n="433" xml:id="pg433"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1491.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 25, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to instructions Nos. 1854 and
                    1473, I now communicate to you, in order that you may be fully in possession of
                    the correspondence on the subject, a copy of a note of the 20th of June, from
                    Sir Frederick Bruce, and of my reply of the 1st instant, in relation to the
                    construction to be placed upon a passage in Earl Russell’s despatch of the 2d of
                    Jane, concerning the twenty-four hours’ rule.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>[For enclosures see correspondence with British legation, current
                        series.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
